    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2HCMwoLCw1KVjty9i7Bahxd)_\n\n## What\n\n- `sp-see-also-show` and `sp-see-also-show-concept` now draw a decorated view (`sp-see-also-view-mode`), laid out like the DG context pane of `discourse-graphs`.\n- A group per concept, open question or litnote: a coloured heading (`outline-1`) with score and counts as small print.\n- An entry per mention: heading line (marks, place, question), then the context as an indented quote.\n- Each entry has a background from `sp-highlight` (the Modus `bg-hl-line`), so it follows the active theme.\n- Headings and contexts are clickable (mouse-1 or `RET`) and visit the footnote; a concept heading opens its concept view.\n- Keys: `n`/`p` headings, `TAB` fold one entry, `S-TAB` fold all, `g` redraw, `q` close.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Literate doc updated (section \"The two views\"); tangling it gives the committed `.el` files exactly.\n- Two ERT tests added; all 27 pass in batch Emacs 29. Not seen in the real GUI with the real vault yet.\n- No `CHANGELOG.org` change (the nightly tidy writes it).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiD1WCz5BjUbXLvPJST)_",
